{
  "name": "07-pending-gate-check-error-override",
  "description": "Complete contract meets the model-checked shipped gate at task.before_ready and answers pending. No orchestrator has polled, so the workspace's Orchestrator offline item opens; the check misses its queue timeout twice and ends in error, which holds the task with check_error and opens no task item; the owner overrides the check once, the hold closes and the pending move to Ready completes with the owner's original key; when the orchestrator polls again the workspace item closes.",
  "covers": [
    "PRD How a transition is gated, steps 5 and 6: a blocking model check stores the pending transition, queues a job, opens a check step and answers pending.",
    "PRD When a check cannot run: a second miss of the queue timeout gives error; an error on a blocking rule leaves the transition pending under check_error; the override closes the hold and the transition completes in place.",
    "PRD Event record, command_id: the completing events carry the original requester's key with cause_id set to the check.finished event.",
    "PRD When a check cannot run, and plan SM-39: while the orchestrator is offline the workspace-level item covers the waiting check and no task item opens for check_error.",
    "Plan TM-1: check_queue_timeout first and second miss and orchestrator_offline run as timers with the app as caller and their due time as effective_at."
  ],
